---
const controls = [
  {
    title: 'Permissions by role and module',
    body: 'Each user sees and does only what their role allows.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Approval limits per branch and product',
    body: 'Applications route to the right authority by your rules.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Full audit trail',
    body: 'Who changed what, and when, on every application.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Credit registry and core banking',
    body: 'Exposure imported from the registry; accounts and payments read from your core system.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Your own scorecards',
    body: 'Internal rating models with knock-out and adjustment criteria.',
  },
  {
    title: '[Deployment and certification]',
    body: '[On-premise in your data centre? ISO 27001? Confirm before publishing.]',
  },
];
---

<section id="controls" class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="runhead" data-reveal>
      <span>Controls</span>
    </div>
    <div class="sec-head" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Built to pass your risk and compliance review.</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">
        The record is the control. Limits, roles and the audit trail are part of how a file moves,
        not reports written afterwards.
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="ctl-grid">
      {
        controls.map((c) => (
          <div class="ctl" data-reveal>
            <dt>{c.title}</dt>
            <dd>{c.body}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>
